<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We further analyzed the extent of coverage—that is, the proportion of canonical code revealed in leaked snippets. These results are reported in Table <a href="#A5.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ Appendix E Data Leakage Analysis ‣ RECODE-H: A Benchmark for Research Code Development with Interactive Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>. Again, leakage is effectively absent at Levels 1-2, minimal at Level 3, and substantially higher at Level 4.</p>
</div>
